## 3. Register the handler when you initialise MapLibre

You only have to do this **once**, before you create any `MapView`/`MapLibreMap`.

```kotlin
package com.example.maplibrevault

import android.app.Application
import org.maplibre.android.MapLibre
import org.maplibre.android.MapLibreOptions

class MyApplication : Application() {

    override fun onCreate() {
        super.onCreate()

        // 1️⃣  Create your vault helper (whatever you need for decryption)
        val vault = TileVault(this)   // <-- your own implementation

        // 2️⃣  Build the MapLibre options with the custom handler
        val options = MapLibreOptions.builder()
            .httpRequestHandler(VaultTileRequestHandler(vault))
            .build()

        // 3️⃣  Initialise the SDK with those options
        MapLibre.getInstance(this, options)
    }
}
```

If you have already called `MapLibre.getInstance(context)` elsewhere you can also replace the handler later:

```kotlin
MapLibre.getInstance(this).setHttpRequestHandler(VaultTileRequestHandler(vault))
```

> **Note** – The SDK uses **OkHttp** under the hood, so the handler runs on a background thread already.  
> Do **not** perform heavy work on the UI thread; keep decryption fast or off‑load to a coroutine/worker if needed.

