## 5. Alternative: OkHttp interceptor (if you already use a custom OkHttp client)

If you prefer to stay in the OkHttp world you can also supply a **custom `OkHttpClient`** that contains an interceptor for the `vault://` scheme:

```kotlin
val client = OkHttpClient.Builder()
    .addInterceptor { chain ->
        val request = chain.request()
        if (request.url.scheme == "vault") {
            // same decryption logic as above …
            val decrypted = ... // ByteArray
            val body = ResponseBody.create(
                MediaType.get("application/vnd.mapbox-vector-tile"),
                decrypted
            )
            Response.Builder()
                .request(request)
                .protocol(Protocol.HTTP_1_1)
                .code(200)
                .message("OK")
                .body(body)
                .build()
        } else {
            chain.proceed(request)   // normal network
        }
    }
    .build()

val options = MapLibreOptions.builder()
    .httpClient(client)   // <--

