## Things to keep in mind

1. **Network permissions** – add `<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>` to your `AndroidManifest.xml` if you haven’t already.

2. **CORS / Tile‑JSON** – The URL you give (`https://example.com/terrain.json`) must return a **TileJSON** document that points to raster‑DEM tiles (usually `*.png` or `*.webp`). The same format the web SDK expects works natively.

3. **Style extensions** – Terrain support lives in the **MapLibre Android SDK extensions** module (`android-sdk-extensions`). If you only depend on `android-sdk`, you’ll get a compile‑time error for `Terrain`. The Gradle line shown at the top adds it.

4. **Exaggeration limits** – Values > 10 can cause visual artefacts on low‑resolution DEMs. Stick to the range 0.0 – 10.0 for best results.

5. **Switching terrain on/off** – If you ever need to remove terrain, call `style.setTerrain(null)`.

6. **Multiple DEM sources** – Only one terrain source can be active at a time. If you add another `RasterDemSource` you must call `style.setTerrain(Terrain(newSourceId))` again.

